{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he said: Alas, who shall live, when El does this.</b> In the chapter חלק, Resh Lakish said: Alas for one who keeps himself alive with a mere El — or alternatively, with a mere Eloha. And Rabbi Yohanan says: Alas for that nation that will be found at the hour when the Holy One, blessed be He, brings redemption for His children. Who would cast his cloak between a lion and a lioness at the hour when they mate with each other? Another interpretation: he was lamenting and saying: Who will be able to survive that 'setting' שימה that the Holy One, blessed be He, will set upon the world? And he prophesied about King Messiah."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:10.821908199Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}